221;.vc_custom_1770382327902{margin-bottom: 30px !important;}&#8221;] Depictions of Colonialism and Power in Media A session with award-winning filmmaker Manfred Becker marked the launch of VIIEW. Becker used films and photographs to explore how history is documented and how colonial legacies continue to shape modern identity. He covered how Western audiences &#8220;consume&#8221; sites of tragedy and conflict, raising&hellip;<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false}},{\"id\":49700,\"slug\":\"mba-in-creative-industries\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/www.whistlingwoods.net\\/programmes\\/mba-in-creative-industries\\/\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"MBA in Creative Industries | (2 Years)\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"<div class=\\\"wpb-content-wrapper\\\" id=\\\"wpb-content-root\\\">\n<strong>Learn in a Dual-Institution Ecosystem<\\/strong>\n<br \\/>\\nLearn how to create, manage, and scale media ventures across film, television, OTT, gaming, animation, and digital platforms.<\\/p>\\n<p>IIM Mumbai, erstwhile known as NITIE, was established by the Government of India in 1963 with the assistance of the United Nations Development Programme (UNDP) and the International Labour Organisation (ILO). IIM Mumbai has been consistently ranked among the top B-schools in India. IIM Mumbai is ranked 6th in the National Institutional Ranking Framework (NIRF) rankings for 2025 among Management Institutes across India. IIM Mumbai is committed to creating skilled professionals in diverse functional areas like Operations Management, Analytics, Finance, Marketing, Project Management, HR, Information Technology, and Sustainability Management.<\\/p>\\n<p>By leveraging its legacy of producing world-class business leaders, IIM Mumbai proudly collaborates with Asia&#8217;s premier institute for film and media education, Whistling Woods International (WWI), to bring transformative education. Both the institutes aim to facilitate learners in advancing innovation, entrepreneurial skills, and strategic thinking, preparing graduates to drive growth in India&#8217;s booming media and entertainment industry, projected to reach $50 billion by 2030.<\\/p>\\n<p>WWI is India&#8217;s premier institute of Film, Communication, Creative &amp; Performing Arts. Founded by one of India&#8217;s leading filmmakers &#8211; Subhash Ghai, WWI has been successfully delivering world-class education in all creative &amp; technical aspects of the Creative Industries Industry since 2006.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \\\">\\n<div class=\\\"wpb_wrapper\\\">\\n<p>\n<br \\/>\\nWhistling Woods International is one of India&#8217;s premier institutes for media, entertainment, design, and creative arts education. Established with a vision to nurture future-ready talent for the global creative economy, the institute offers industry-aligned programs across filmmaking, animation, media management, fashion, music, acting, and emerging digital domains. Known for its world-class infrastructure, strong industry linkages, and hands-on learning approach, Whistling Woods International has built a reputation for producing professionals who excel across leading creative industries in India and beyond.<\\/p>\\n<p>\n<br \\/>\\nIndian Institute of Management Mumbai is one of India&#8217;s leading management institutions, recognized for academic excellence, rigorous pedagogy, and strong industry relevance. With a legacy of developing future leaders in management, operations, analytics, and public policy, the institute combines cutting-edge research with practical business education. IIM Mumbai is committed to shaping professionals who can lead organizations in a rapidly evolving global economy through innovation, strategic thinking, and responsible leadership.<\\/p>\\n<p>\n<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Applicants must hold a Bachelor\\u2019s Degree in any discipline<\\/li>\\n<li>Minimum 50% marks or equivalent CGPA (45% for SC\\/ST\\/PwD candidates)<\\/li>\\n<li>Degree must be from a recognised university\\/institution as per UGC\\/Ministry of Education norms<\\/li>\\n<li>Candidates should submit a valid CAT, GRE, or GMAT score or appear for the Creative Industries IMAT exam<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>\n<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Withdrawal before programme commencement &#8211; Fee refunded after a deduction of \\u20b91,000<\\/li>\\n<li>Withdrawal after commencement of classes &#8211; No refund applicable<\\/li>\\n<li>Refunds, if applicable, are processed as per the institute&#8217;s guidelines<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>[\\/vc_column_text][\\/vc_tab][\\/vc_tabs][\\/vc_column][\\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_raw_js][\\/vc_raw_js][\\/vc_column][\\/vc_row]<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\",\"protected\":false},\"excerpt\":{\"rendered\":\"<p>[vc_row css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1758096691416{margin-bottom: 15px !important;}&#8221;][vc_column][vc_single_image image=&#8221;50234&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221;][vc_row_inner content_placement=&#8221;middle&#8221;][vc_column_inner width=&#8221;4\\/5&#8243;][vc_column_text el_class=&#8221;admission-details&#8221;] About Programme [\\/vc_column_text][\\/vc_column_inner][vc_column_inner width=&#8221;1\\/5&#8243;][vc_column_text]Register Now[\\/vc_column_text][\\/vc_column_inner][\\/vc_row_inner][\\/vc_column][\\/vc_row][vc_row el_class=&#8221;admission-details&#8221;][vc_column][vc_tabs][vc_tab title=&#8221;OVERVIEW&#8221; tab_id=&#8221;1656570382025-3-05b9e-781c&#8221;][vc_column_text] First-of-its-Kind Programme from IIM Mumbai The programme, the first of its kind among IIMs in India, is jointly developed with Whistling Woods International to meet the evolving demands of the global media and entertainment industry. Where Business Meets&hellip;<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false}},{\"id\":49469,\"slug\":\"september-4-2025-guest-session-with-yash-dhar-alumni-on-how-to-hold-emotions-and-qa-about-jobs-of-assistant-editors-in-the-indian-film-industry-with-the-school-of-filmmaking-students\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/www.whistlingwoods.net\\/do-what-you-love\\/workshops\\/september-4-2025-guest-session-with-yash-dhar-alumni-on-how-to-hold-emotions-and-qa-about-jobs-of-assistant-editors-in-the-indian-film-industry-with-the-school-of-filmmaking-students\\/\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"September 4, 2025: Guest Session with Yash Dhar (Alumni) on How to Hold Emotions and Q&#038;A about Jobs of Assistant Editors in the Indian Film Industry with the School of Filmmaking Students\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"<div class=\\\"wpb-content-wrapper\\\" id=\\\"wpb-content-root\\\">\n<\\/div>[\\/vc_column][\\/vc_row]<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\",\"protected\":false},\"excerpt\":{\"rendered\":\"<p>[vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1756709504352{margin-bottom: 30px !important;}&#8221;][\\/vc_column_text][\\/vc_column][\\/vc_row]<\\/p>\\n\",\"protected\":false}},{\"id\":49056,\"slug\":\"alumni-success\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/www.whistlingwoods.net\\/alumni-success\\/\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"Alumni Success\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"<div class=\\\"wpb-content-wrapper\\\" id=\\\"wpb-content-root\\\">\n<\\/p>\\n<p>[\\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text el_class=&#8221;news-media-title&#8221; css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1660903433071{background-color: #ffffff !important;}&#8221;][\\/vc_column_text][\\/vc_column][\\/vc_row]<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\",\"protected\":false},\"excerpt\":{\"rendered\":\"<p>[vc_row full_width=&#8221;stretch_row&#8221; bg_type=&#8221;image&#8221; parallax_style=&#8221;vcpb-default&#8221; bg_image_repeat=&#8221;no-repeat&#8221; el_id=&#8221;about&#8221; css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1644570531208{padding-bottom: 30px !important;}&#8221;][vc_column css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1644570413984{padding-top: 4px !important;padding-bottom: 4px !important;background-color: #ffffff !important;}&#8221;][vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1754043198976{margin-top: 15px !important;margin-right: 10px !important;margin-bottom: 25px !important;margin-left: 10px !important;background-color: #ffffff !important;}&#8221;] [\\/vc_column_text][